  "worked_solution": "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,\u2713 \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-4\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=4\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only ${b}_{1}$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$",
